{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H04 — Cross-module public interface split\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Cross-module refactor (2/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic catalog program with three\nmodules:\n\n- `catalog.model` — defines the public `Item` type, its constructor, and one\n  **combined** public helper `adjust(item, qty_delta, price_delta)` that\n  returns an item with both quantity and price adjusted;\n- `orders.build` — calls the combined helper with a quantity delta (price\n  delta 0) to reserve stock;\n- `invoice.render` — calls the combined helper with a price delta (quantity\n  delta 0) to render a line.\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H04_SCENARIO` and prints\ndeterministic lines. There is **no persistence** (no serialization, no version\nmarker, no restart, no old-state migration), no wall-clock dependency, and no\nstate machine.\n\n## Required change\n\nSplit the combined public helper in `catalog.model` into **two explicit\npublic operations**:\n\n1. `adjust_qty(item, qty_delta)` — adjusts only the quantity;\n2. `adjust_price(item, price_delta)` — adjusts only the price.\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- both new operations become official public exports of `catalog.model`;\n- `orders.build` migrates to `adjust_qty`;\n- `invoice.render` migrates to `adjust_price`;\n- the old combined `adjust` is **no longer a valid public API**;\n- the `Item` type and its constructor contract stay unchanged (no new fields,\n  no field renames);\n- behavior must remain **exactly identical** (same outputs for the same\n  inputs).\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier rebuilds the project, drives the compiled program through\nscenarios, and additionally checks **external integration consumers**:\n\n- consumers calling `adjust_qty` and `adjust_price` must compile and behave\n  correctly;\n- a consumer still calling the old combined `adjust` must fail to compile\n  against the new public surface;\n- order / invoice behavior must be unchanged.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
